# MMDonkeyKong language file – English (reference / template)
#
# How to add a new language (no recompiling needed):
#   1. Copy this file and name it by the language code, e.g. "fr.lang", "pl.lang", "pt-BR.lang".
#   2. Translate the text after "=" on every line. Keep the key before "=" unchanged.
#   3. Keep placeholders in curly braces, e.g. {error}, unchanged (their order may change).
#   4. Put the file into "lang" next to mmdonkeykong.exe or into %APPDATA%\MMDonkeyKong\lang
#      (Linux: ~/.config/MMDonkeyKong/lang).
#   5. In the program choose View → Language → Reload language files, then pick the language.
#
